1
00:02:57,440 --> 00:02:58,960
Is that you, Sarai?

2
00:03:03,160 --> 00:03:04,679
You must die.

3
00:03:04,680 --> 00:03:05,800
Sarai.

4
00:03:08,800 --> 00:03:10,080
I miss my mom.

5
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:19,800
I want to see my mom.

6
00:03:35,720 --> 00:03:37,480
Where is she?

7
00:03:39,680 --> 00:03:42,080
She was so quick.

8
00:04:23,840 --> 00:04:27,000
Mr. Narathon.

9
00:04:28,720 --> 00:04:29,720
This is Mr. Phum's.

10
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:32,400
Thank you.

11
00:04:35,040 --> 00:04:36,680
Please take care of my father.

12
00:04:37,280 --> 00:04:39,559
I'm going home to change clothes,
then I'll come back.

13
00:04:39,560 --> 00:04:43,879
Yes. He still has to wait for the doctor
before being transferred to a room.

14
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:45,680
It'll probably be late in the morning.

15
00:04:46,320 --> 00:04:47,280
Thank you.

16
00:05:40,640 --> 00:05:41,680
Hello?

17
00:05:44,560 --> 00:05:45,680
Yes.

18
00:05:52,520 --> 00:05:56,800
Mr. Narathon said Mr. Phum will be moved
to a private room later this morning.

19
00:05:59,640 --> 00:06:02,560
Then we'll visit him this afternoon.

20
00:06:03,160 --> 00:06:04,400
Yes.

21
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,439
Good morning.

22
00:06:13,440 --> 00:06:14,840
Da, good morning.

23
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:17,720
Oh, Da.

24
00:06:21,760 --> 00:06:22,920
Hello, Auntie.

25
00:06:24,560 --> 00:06:25,840
Hello, Uncle.

26
00:06:30,920 --> 00:06:32,120
Hello, Mook.

27
00:06:35,520 --> 00:06:38,240
Where's Na?

28
00:06:39,760 --> 00:06:41,600
He'll probably come later.

29
00:06:43,440 --> 00:06:45,560
It's been a long time, Prawin.

30
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:50,280
Yes. But you're still
as beautiful as ever, Auntie.

31
00:06:51,120 --> 00:06:54,080
And Uncle hasn't aged a day.

32
00:06:57,640 --> 00:07:01,519
I want to come talk to Na.

33
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:04,920
I want to have a six-pack like him,
but I never have time.

34
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:18,959
I'm really sorry, Mook.
I tried to stop him.

35
00:07:18,960 --> 00:07:21,119
But Win insisted on coming to see you.

36
00:07:21,120 --> 00:07:25,759
He said he'd do anything
to make you forgive him.

37
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:28,560
Because he just realized
he can't live without you.

38
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:34,639
So dramatic.
I'm not going along with his nonsense.

39
00:07:34,640 --> 00:07:37,479
Thank goodness Na showed up in time.

40
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:39,679
He started talking to Win about fitness.

41
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:42,760
Otherwise,
he'd still be following me around.

42
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,119
Take care of it.

43
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:50,560
It's urgent, okay?

44
00:07:51,200 --> 00:07:53,320
Oh, good morning, Mr. Narathon.

45
00:07:53,960 --> 00:07:56,000
Mr. Phum hasn't come in yet.

46
00:07:57,360 --> 00:08:00,000
My father was in an accident.

47
00:08:01,400 --> 00:08:03,040
Is it serious?

48
00:08:03,640 --> 00:08:08,279
He's still in the hospital.
He'll probably be away for quite a while.

49
00:08:08,280 --> 00:08:12,559
Please take care of all his appointments.

50
00:08:12,560 --> 00:08:15,959
Of course. I'll handle everything.

51
00:08:15,960 --> 00:08:17,480
Don't worry.

52
00:08:18,480 --> 00:08:20,079
As for Pakarang...

53
00:08:20,080 --> 00:08:22,840
Ms. Pakarang hasn't come in today either.

54
00:08:23,880 --> 00:08:26,560
She's at the hospital too.

55
00:08:27,280 --> 00:08:28,680
What?

56
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:33,559
She was with my father.
Fortunately, she wasn't seriously injured.

57
00:08:34,360 --> 00:08:36,439
What a relief.

58
00:08:36,440 --> 00:08:40,280
Please try to contact her relatives.

59
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:44,759
Ms. Pakarang doesn't have any relatives.

60
00:08:44,760 --> 00:08:47,200
Mr. Phum was even hiring
a private investigator...

61
00:08:49,360 --> 00:08:50,520
Oops.

62
00:08:53,280 --> 00:08:54,880
What did you say?

63
00:08:55,800 --> 00:08:58,400
Nothing.

64
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:39,480
<i>Mr. Narathon.</i>

65
00:09:40,880 --> 00:09:41,720
Yes?

66
00:09:42,440 --> 00:09:44,200
<i>Ms. Mook wants to see you.</i>

67
00:09:45,320 --> 00:09:46,800
Please send her in.

68
00:09:58,240 --> 00:10:00,080
Is something wrong?

69
00:10:01,320 --> 00:10:03,960
I was completely wrong
about my father and Pakarang.

70
00:10:04,680 --> 00:10:05,960
How?

71
00:10:07,360 --> 00:10:11,200
Pakarang was in a boating accident.

72
00:10:12,240 --> 00:10:14,360
Dad saved her life.

73
00:10:14,960 --> 00:10:17,920
She lost her memory,
so Dad brought her here

74
00:10:18,520 --> 00:10:22,079
to take care of her and has been trying

75
00:10:22,080 --> 00:10:23,960
to find her real family.

76
00:10:27,160 --> 00:10:30,760
Maybe I've been too pessimistic about him.

77
00:10:33,360 --> 00:10:37,400
Don't overthink. You only thought that
because of what happened to Sarai.

78
00:10:38,480 --> 00:10:41,399
Hearing all this makes it even harder

79
00:10:41,400 --> 00:10:43,319
for me to believe
that a good man like Mr. Phum

80
00:10:43,320 --> 00:10:45,560
could have killed Sarai.

81
00:10:47,840 --> 00:10:50,239
We need to find evidence quickly.

82
00:10:50,240 --> 00:10:52,240
Then this whole thing
can finally be resolved.

83
00:10:52,840 --> 00:10:55,719
And you won't have to
carry this burden anymore.

84
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:57,120
Evidence.

85
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:06,600
What key is that?

86
00:11:08,880 --> 00:11:11,800
Probably Dad's desk key.

87
00:11:13,840 --> 00:11:17,240
Maybe the evidence is in here.

88
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,519
I'm here to see Mr. Phum.
Which room is he in?

89
00:11:37,520 --> 00:11:39,800
- Mr. Phum Witassanai?
- Who are you?

90
00:11:43,480 --> 00:11:44,960
And who are you?

91
00:11:45,760 --> 00:11:47,280
I'm Mr. Phum's wife.

92
00:11:48,000 --> 00:11:49,120
Wife?

93
00:11:52,800 --> 00:11:55,959
Didn't your parents teach you

94
00:11:55,960 --> 00:11:58,680
that laughing outside an ICU
is inappropriate?

95
00:12:01,040 --> 00:12:03,079
You're getting a little out of line.

96
00:12:03,080 --> 00:12:04,760
Do you even know who I am to Mr. Phum?

97
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:12,519
Someone like you
must be his temporary woman.

98
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,120
You'll never be his wife like me.

99
00:12:16,120 --> 00:12:17,600
With such an ordinary face,

100
00:12:18,640 --> 00:12:22,160
you're probably nothing
more than a mistress.

101
00:12:27,280 --> 00:12:28,199
How does it feel?

102
00:12:28,200 --> 00:12:32,480
Getting slapped might finally teach you
to watch your mouth.

103
00:12:33,080 --> 00:12:35,960
Nobody slaps me for free.

104
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:45,199
- What's your problem?!
- Please stop.

105
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:46,879
- What's your problem?!
- Ma'am.

106
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:48,999
Ma'am, please stop.

107
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:50,199
Please don't fight here.

108
00:12:50,200 --> 00:12:52,400
Please.

109
00:12:57,480 --> 00:12:58,640
This is an order.

110
00:12:59,320 --> 00:13:02,160
As Mr. Phum's wife,

111
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:06,879
I forbid this woman
from visiting my husband.

112
00:13:06,880 --> 00:13:09,200
If you let her in,
I'll make sure there are consequences.

113
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,040
- Is that woman Mr. Phum's wife?
- Yes.

114
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:20,720
How many more women are you going to have?

115
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,440
How could you do this to me?

116
00:14:29,360 --> 00:14:31,639
I won't let you go, Mr. Phum.

117
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:34,720
Mr. Phum. Mr. Phum.

118
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:38,919
Are you crazy? I'm going to work.

119
00:14:38,920 --> 00:14:41,160
I have to host a dinner for Mr. Kim.

120
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:42,920
I don't believe you.

121
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:44,759
It's because I'm pregnant?

122
00:14:44,760 --> 00:14:46,400
That's why you're looking for scraps
somewhere else.

123
00:14:47,680 --> 00:14:49,680
That's too much.

124
00:14:50,960 --> 00:14:52,600
I won't let you go.

125
00:14:53,520 --> 00:14:55,399
So why did you let yourself get pregnant?

126
00:14:55,400 --> 00:14:57,240
I told you I didn't want another child.

127
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,800
Having Thon is enough for me.

128
00:15:00,520 --> 00:15:01,919
But I want to have a child with you.

129
00:15:01,920 --> 00:15:03,879
Mr. Phum, I won't let you go.

130
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:05,039
Hey.

131
00:15:05,040 --> 00:15:06,999
This is too much. I'm late now.

132
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:09,839
I'm not letting you go.

133
00:15:09,840 --> 00:15:11,000
I'm late now.

134
00:15:15,200 --> 00:15:16,120
Sairung.

135
00:15:18,760 --> 00:15:19,800
Sairung.

136
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:55,440
You must be satisfied now, right?

137
00:15:56,400 --> 00:15:58,320
My baby is dead.

138
00:15:59,840 --> 00:16:01,360
I didn't mean for this to happen.

139
00:16:05,480 --> 00:16:07,920
You never wanted that child
in the first place.

140
00:16:10,760 --> 00:16:14,960
But I never thought of hurting the child.
It was an accident.

141
00:16:16,560 --> 00:16:20,320
I'm sorry.
I'll make it up to you in every way.

142
00:16:20,880 --> 00:16:23,360
Whatever you want, tell me.

143
00:16:24,600 --> 00:16:27,720
Except for
having another child. I beg you.

144
00:16:28,600 --> 00:16:31,000
I don't want Narathon to be hurt
any more than he already has been.

145
00:16:31,920 --> 00:16:33,600
I've already wronged him enough.

146
00:16:45,520 --> 00:16:46,760
Fine.

147
00:16:47,640 --> 00:16:49,920
If you don't want to have a child with me,

148
00:16:52,560 --> 00:16:54,720
then you must promise me

149
00:16:55,440 --> 00:16:57,840
that you will never have a child
with any other woman either.

150
00:16:59,960 --> 00:17:01,080
I promise.

151
00:17:03,040 --> 00:17:04,839
If you break your word,

152
00:17:06,520 --> 00:17:08,480
I'll kill both that woman

153
00:17:09,480 --> 00:17:12,960
and her child. Just you wait.

154
00:17:20,680 --> 00:17:21,960
In the end,

155
00:17:22,520 --> 00:17:24,560
you broke your promise to me.

156
00:17:25,839 --> 00:17:28,000
You had a child with Sarai after all.

157
00:17:37,920 --> 00:17:40,520
I've put up with you long enough.

158
00:19:14,680 --> 00:19:16,440
What document is that?

159
00:19:18,480 --> 00:19:19,960
My father's will.

160
00:19:29,520 --> 00:19:31,880
Mr. Phum really loves you.

161
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,440
He leaves everything to you alone.

162
00:19:40,320 --> 00:19:44,000
Mr. Narathon,
look at the note at the end of the will.

163
00:19:51,920 --> 00:19:56,319
"If Sarai, my last wife, ever returns,

164
00:19:56,320 --> 00:19:59,239
Narathon must help and take care of her

165
00:19:59,240 --> 00:20:01,200
as if I were still alive."

166
00:20:03,840 --> 00:20:06,200
It's like
he still doesn't know Sarai is dead.

167
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:14,760
That means
Mr. Phum wasn't the one who killed her.

168
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:22,920
Then who killed Sarai?

169
00:20:31,960 --> 00:20:33,480
Just a little more

170
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:37,280
and you'll be in hell

171
00:20:37,880 --> 00:20:40,120
with your precious Sarai.

172
00:20:42,160 --> 00:20:43,800
Tell her

173
00:20:44,920 --> 00:20:46,720
I ask for forgiveness.

174
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:55,440
I really had no choice.
She stole you from me.

175
00:20:56,480 --> 00:20:58,920
That's why she and her child
ended up like that.

176
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:06,880
Sairung.

177
00:21:09,320 --> 00:21:10,680
Does that mean...?

178
00:21:16,200 --> 00:21:19,959
No, Mr. Phum. Don't die.

179
00:21:19,960 --> 00:21:21,520
Mr. Phum.

180
00:21:31,360 --> 00:21:32,960
Nurse.

181
00:21:34,080 --> 00:21:36,159
Something's wrong with Mr. Phum.

182
00:21:36,160 --> 00:21:39,199
Please help. Hurry.

183
00:21:39,200 --> 00:21:41,800
I'm sorry. The ventilator came loose.

184
00:21:44,520 --> 00:21:47,319
I'll check who was on duty.

185
00:21:47,320 --> 00:21:48,240
Okay.

186
00:21:48,840 --> 00:21:50,400
Oh, it's alright,

187
00:21:51,360 --> 00:21:54,639
as long as Mr. Phum is safe.

188
00:21:54,640 --> 00:21:56,920
Alright. The doctor will be here soon.

189
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:46,080
I'm sorry...

190
00:22:53,920 --> 00:22:56,160
I misunderstood you all this time.

191
00:23:53,280 --> 00:23:54,520
What?

192
00:23:57,120 --> 00:24:00,360
Hey, nurse,
aren't you going to do something?

193
00:24:02,880 --> 00:24:03,880
Hey.

194
00:24:11,800 --> 00:24:15,079
Help me. Is someone there?

195
00:24:15,080 --> 00:24:18,360
Is someone there? Help me!

196
00:24:19,280 --> 00:24:20,560
Help me!

197
00:24:37,720 --> 00:24:39,560
You remember me, don't you?

198
00:24:42,760 --> 00:24:44,040
Sarai.

199
00:24:45,640 --> 00:24:49,319
You're already dead.
Why are you still haunting me?

200
00:24:49,320 --> 00:24:50,760
Why did you kill me?

201
00:24:53,280 --> 00:24:54,760
I don't know anything.

202
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:56,840
You must pay for what you did.

203
00:25:39,920 --> 00:25:42,599
Ma'am. Are you alright, ma'am?

204
00:25:42,600 --> 00:25:45,919
Take a deep breath. Nurse!

205
00:25:45,920 --> 00:25:47,759
Someone's unwell here.

206
00:25:47,760 --> 00:25:50,000
- Nurse.
- I'm fine.

207
00:25:54,040 --> 00:25:55,280
Are you alright?

208
00:26:32,320 --> 00:26:36,520
Did you think you could escape me?
Keep driving.

209
00:26:37,720 --> 00:26:40,520
Where are you taking me? I'm not going.

210
00:26:49,840 --> 00:26:54,000
No! I'm not going. I'm not going!

211
00:26:56,680 --> 00:26:58,480
I'm not going. Help me!

212
00:27:36,480 --> 00:27:39,480
Don't hurt me, Sarai. Please let me go.

213
00:27:40,480 --> 00:27:42,720
Let you go? Fine.

214
00:27:45,280 --> 00:27:47,760
No. Sarai.

215
00:27:48,360 --> 00:27:49,600
No.

216
00:27:51,160 --> 00:27:53,120
Please let me go!

217
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:06,360
Sarai, you can't do this to me.

218
00:28:07,240 --> 00:28:08,920
I took you in and raised you.

219
00:28:09,680 --> 00:28:12,520
You were the ungrateful one
who stole my husband.

220
00:28:14,120 --> 00:28:18,200
But I left Mr. Phum as you ordered.

221
00:28:19,320 --> 00:28:23,360
Why did you still send someone to kill me?
Why?!

222
00:28:23,960 --> 00:28:27,439
I didn't kill you. They did it.

223
00:28:27,440 --> 00:28:29,920
I knew nothing.

224
00:28:31,480 --> 00:28:32,720
Do you know

225
00:28:33,960 --> 00:28:36,799
how much I suffered

226
00:28:36,800 --> 00:28:39,280
under the sea?

227
00:28:40,040 --> 00:28:42,199
I'll make you know

228
00:28:42,200 --> 00:28:44,400
what that feels like too.

229
00:28:45,520 --> 00:28:50,040
No. Please let me go.

230
00:28:51,040 --> 00:28:53,679
I'll repay you for everything.

231
00:28:53,680 --> 00:28:54,839
Let me go.

232
00:28:54,840 --> 00:28:56,040
No!

233
00:28:57,840 --> 00:29:00,400
I was torn away from my child

234
00:29:01,360 --> 00:29:02,880
because of you.

235
00:29:05,160 --> 00:29:07,760
I had to suffer, searching for my child,

236
00:29:08,680 --> 00:29:11,960
never knowing
whether my child was alive or dead!

237
00:29:13,240 --> 00:29:17,999
Let me go. I'll repay you!

238
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:22,479
I'll make a lot of merit for you.
I'll help you be reborn.

239
00:29:22,480 --> 00:29:25,960
Please let me go.

240
00:29:27,080 --> 00:29:30,040
Do you know the taste of fear now?

241
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:51,160
Please let me go. I'm begging you!

242
00:29:52,600 --> 00:29:56,519
I'll make merit for you.

243
00:29:56,520 --> 00:29:58,439
I'll find your child.

244
00:29:58,440 --> 00:30:01,400
I promise.

245
00:30:02,080 --> 00:30:03,080
My child...

246
00:30:11,120 --> 00:30:12,720
Where is my child?

247
00:30:13,320 --> 00:30:17,080
I don't know, but I'll find them.

248
00:30:18,400 --> 00:30:21,760
I'm telling the truth. I know I was wrong.

249
00:30:22,680 --> 00:30:25,040
Give me a chance.

250
00:30:26,080 --> 00:30:28,519
I'll find your child.

251
00:30:28,520 --> 00:30:32,360
If I can't,

252
00:30:33,160 --> 00:30:37,079
you can come kill me,

253
00:30:37,080 --> 00:30:39,680
and I'll accept it.

254
00:30:40,280 --> 00:30:41,240
Please.

255
00:30:44,760 --> 00:30:46,720
I'll give you one chance.

256
00:30:51,200 --> 00:30:54,560
Thank you, Sarai. Thank you so much.

257
00:30:56,000 --> 00:30:57,720
Within three days,

258
00:30:59,320 --> 00:31:01,440
if you can't find my child,

259
00:31:02,520 --> 00:31:04,000
I'll kill you.

260
00:31:27,920 --> 00:31:29,920
I'm scared! I'm scared!

261
00:32:48,400 --> 00:32:50,400
I'm sorry, Mr. Phum.

262
00:32:55,120 --> 00:32:57,280
You ended up like this

263
00:32:59,640 --> 00:33:01,480
because of my foolishness

264
00:33:03,960 --> 00:33:06,680
and my misunderstanding.

265
00:33:13,680 --> 00:33:15,320
I'll help take care of you

266
00:33:17,240 --> 00:33:18,920
until you recover.

267
00:33:27,560 --> 00:33:29,280
Which room is Mr. Phum in?

268
00:33:30,560 --> 00:33:31,639
Thank you.

269
00:33:31,640 --> 00:33:33,040
- Thank you.
- Let's go, Da.

270
00:33:45,200 --> 00:33:46,960
He's still asleep.

271
00:33:47,960 --> 00:33:49,479
Oh, really?

272
00:33:49,480 --> 00:33:50,920
Then...

273
00:33:57,480 --> 00:33:58,600
What is it, Da?

274
00:34:00,520 --> 00:34:01,800
Let's go.

275
00:34:37,159 --> 00:34:38,199
Win.

276
00:34:39,520 --> 00:34:40,520
Win.

277
00:34:41,719 --> 00:34:42,920
Wake up.

278
00:34:49,120 --> 00:34:52,760
Why are you lying here?
Why don't you go see Kaimook?

279
00:34:54,600 --> 00:34:55,719
I went.

280
00:34:57,080 --> 00:34:58,320
Did you get anything?

281
00:35:03,080 --> 00:35:05,079
I might have,

282
00:35:05,080 --> 00:35:08,960
if Kaimook's brother Mana
hadn't dragged me off to work out first.

283
00:35:11,880 --> 00:35:13,600
So basically, you got nothing.

284
00:35:15,520 --> 00:35:17,600
I really put my hopes in the wrong person.

285
00:35:19,560 --> 00:35:23,879
Calm down, Pat. Why are you so upset?

286
00:35:23,880 --> 00:35:26,079
Of course I'm upset.

287
00:35:26,080 --> 00:35:29,039
Now Mr. Phum has had an accident
and is in the hospital.

288
00:35:29,040 --> 00:35:31,719
The gallery opening
will be postponed indefinitely.

289
00:35:31,720 --> 00:35:34,639
So when am I supposed to meet Kaimook?

290
00:35:34,640 --> 00:35:38,320
I was counting on you,
but you're useless too.

291
00:35:40,320 --> 00:35:41,400
Oh, Pat.

292
00:35:42,560 --> 00:35:44,519
Actually, I think I know

293
00:35:44,520 --> 00:35:48,760
where Kaimook took that Black Coral photo.

294
00:35:51,640 --> 00:35:53,240
You really know?

295
00:35:55,160 --> 00:35:59,199
Not only do I know,
I've been there before.

296
00:35:59,200 --> 00:36:02,239
And I'm sure that's the place.

297
00:36:02,240 --> 00:36:03,640
Where?

298
00:36:04,800 --> 00:36:06,000
Skull Island.

299
00:36:06,840 --> 00:36:08,040
Skull Island?

300
00:37:05,320 --> 00:37:07,280
I'm about to return to my original form.

301
00:37:12,040 --> 00:37:15,320
In two more nights,
it will be the night of the dark moon.

302
00:37:17,720 --> 00:37:21,480
The day when the power
of evil is at its strongest.

303
00:37:22,560 --> 00:37:25,600
I must perform
the final ritual that night.

304
00:37:26,800 --> 00:37:29,919
I need the lives
of two more humans as offerings.

305
00:37:29,920 --> 00:37:31,920
Go find them quickly.

306
00:37:32,520 --> 00:37:35,960
But no boats dare pass this way now.

307
00:37:36,640 --> 00:37:38,360
Where am I supposed to find anyone?

308
00:38:01,600 --> 00:38:03,880
I heard you! Stop banging!

309
00:38:07,200 --> 00:38:08,160
Ms. Sairung?

310
00:38:20,680 --> 00:38:22,040
What do you want?

311
00:38:27,760 --> 00:38:29,119
What the hell?

312
00:38:29,120 --> 00:38:30,440
What kind of job did you do?

313
00:38:31,520 --> 00:38:33,240
I almost died.

314
00:38:34,840 --> 00:38:37,040
What? What are you talking about?

315
00:38:38,520 --> 00:38:39,920
It's Sarai.

316
00:38:51,720 --> 00:38:55,160
- Maybe you dreamed it.
- Dreamed what?

317
00:38:56,960 --> 00:38:59,999
She attacked me
and brought me all the way here.

318
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:02,200
She was trying to drag me down
to the bottom of the sea with her.

319
00:39:04,880 --> 00:39:08,559
Didn't you say your friend
had trapped her spirit.

320
00:39:08,560 --> 00:39:10,800
Then how did it get out and come after me?

321
00:39:14,240 --> 00:39:15,400
How is that possible?

322
00:39:16,000 --> 00:39:17,240
It already happened.

323
00:39:18,960 --> 00:39:22,440
I almost got killed.
Good thing I survived.

324
00:39:25,120 --> 00:39:26,080
You have to help me.

325
00:39:29,720 --> 00:39:30,880
How am I supposed to help?

326
00:39:31,960 --> 00:39:33,240
Kill her again?

327
00:39:34,160 --> 00:39:36,560
She's a ghost now, not a person.

328
00:39:37,560 --> 00:39:39,359
Don't be stupid.

329
00:39:39,360 --> 00:39:41,119
Go find your friend.

330
00:39:41,120 --> 00:39:44,000
Trap her spirit
and lock her beneath the sea again.

331
00:39:48,240 --> 00:39:49,880
If she finds out
you were the one who killed her,

332
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:52,720
she'll come for you too.

333
00:40:07,560 --> 00:40:09,479
Where are Mom and Dad?

334
00:40:09,480 --> 00:40:13,360
They left. Mr. Phum was still asleep.

335
00:40:15,000 --> 00:40:16,480
What took you so long, Mook?

336
00:40:17,200 --> 00:40:21,440
As soon as I got your call, Mr. Narathon
and I left the company right away.

337
00:40:26,120 --> 00:40:27,280
What's wrong?

338
00:40:32,880 --> 00:40:35,120
I saw that woman ghost.

339
00:40:38,680 --> 00:40:39,680
Where?

340
00:40:42,360 --> 00:40:43,680
In Mr. Phum's room.

341
00:40:45,680 --> 00:40:50,880
But this time, she wasn't looking
at Mr. Phum with hatred like she did.

342
00:40:51,680 --> 00:40:55,560
She was crying
like she regretted something.

343
00:41:02,040 --> 00:41:03,880
Or Sarai knows the truth now?

344
00:41:07,600 --> 00:41:11,639
Ms. Da, can you help me contact Sarai?

345
00:41:11,640 --> 00:41:13,520
There's something I need to ask her.

346
00:41:35,400 --> 00:41:37,680
Okay. I'll try.

347
00:42:04,080 --> 00:42:05,080
Please come in.

348
00:42:24,040 --> 00:42:25,840
She's not here anymore.

349
00:42:29,160 --> 00:42:32,080
Can you try again, please?

350
00:42:34,760 --> 00:42:37,880
She's definitely not here.
I can't see her anywhere.

351
00:42:45,640 --> 00:42:47,640
I'm sorry, Mr. Narathon.

352
00:42:51,720 --> 00:42:55,480
It's not your fault.

353
00:43:04,560 --> 00:43:05,920
Sarai,

354
00:43:08,040 --> 00:43:09,640
where are you?

355
00:43:23,520 --> 00:43:24,719
What are you doing?

356
00:43:24,720 --> 00:43:26,239
I'm going to visit Mr. Phum.

357
00:43:26,240 --> 00:43:29,400
But you're still receiving fluids.
You can't remove the IV yourself.

358
00:43:31,160 --> 00:43:33,879
Why is the fluid level exactly the same?

359
00:43:33,880 --> 00:43:36,079
Wait.

360
00:43:36,080 --> 00:43:39,920
Your body is freezing cold.
Please lie down. I'll get the doctor.

361
00:43:40,520 --> 00:43:43,560
No. I said I'm fine.

362
00:43:47,560 --> 00:43:50,680
She doesn't look like someone
who was just in a serious accident at all.

363
00:43:56,520 --> 00:44:00,200
Ms. Sarai, are you in this room?

364
00:44:01,320 --> 00:44:02,800
Can you hear me?

365
00:44:06,880 --> 00:44:08,680
If you're still here,

366
00:44:11,640 --> 00:44:13,480
please give me a sign.

367
00:44:30,720 --> 00:44:34,039
The Black Coral is Sarai's bones?

368
00:44:34,040 --> 00:44:35,640
If you don't help...

369
00:44:36,760 --> 00:44:37,960
...you'll die too.

370
00:44:40,640 --> 00:44:41,800
Leave!

371
00:44:46,840 --> 00:44:48,439
<i>Sairung</i>

372
00:44:48,440 --> 00:44:50,560
was behind everything.

373
00:45:25,040 --> 00:45:27,280
Subtitle translation by: Panuwat Baikeawon
